    "body": "**Problem:** The mempool estimator added in #34075 checks mempool health by comparing the weight of transactions removed from our mempool with the weight of recently mined blocks.\r\n`removeForBlock` matches block transactions by txid, which does not commit to witness data.\r\nIf a block confirms a lighter witness variant than the one in our mempool, the estimator counts our heavier variant, so the health check can pass even when the matched transactions make up less than 75% of the mined weight.\r\nA heavier mined variant has the opposite effect and understates coverage.\r\nSame-txid witness variants also came up in #35501.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Count each matched transaction's weight from the connected block instead.\r\n`removeForBlock` returns matches in block order, so the estimator can walk the block and the removed entries together.\r\nThe new test first records the false healthy result, then the corrected low-coverage result.\r\n#36182 falls back to block policy for combined estimates when the mempool estimator cannot produce an estimate, but a false healthy result never reaches that fallback.\r\n",
